2,"fn":null,"pn":0}],"title":"Australia-Trade balance-Goods/Services Imports","name":"Goods/Services Imports","titleAt":1701909000000,"about":"Balance of payments is a set of accounts recording all economic transactionsbetween the residents of the country and the rest of the world in a given periodof time, usually one year. Payments into the country are called credits,payments out of the country are called debits. There are three main componentsof a balance of payments: - current account - capital account - financialaccount Either a surplus or a deficit can be shown in any of these components.Current account records the values of the following:-trade balance -exports andimports of goods and services -income payments and expenditure -interest,dividends, salaries -unilateral transfers -aid, taxes, one-way gifts It showshow a country deals with the global economy on a non-investment basis. Goods andservices - debit represents imports of goods and services which consist oftransactions in goods and services (purchases, barter, gifts","source":"Stats AU","unit":"%","imp":-1,"next":null,"stats":{"n":96,"since":"2016-01-07","withForecast":0,"all":{"n":0,"above":0,"below":0,"inline":0},"last12":{"n":0,"above":0,"below":0,"inline":0},"streak":null,"high":{"a":"15%","t":1649295000000,"period":"Feb. 2022"},"low":{"a":"-10%","t":1680744600000,"period":"Feb. 2023"},"avgSurprise":null,"avg5y":1.54,"freq":"monthly"},"slug":"au-australia-trade-balance-goods-services-imports","category":"trd"}